  "note": "Arabic ẓ and Akkadian ṣ correspond in the words for thirst. The Arabic spelling distinguishes an older sound behind Hebrew צ. The Peshitta commonly uses צהא for thirst. Its middle consonant differs, and its derivation is uncertain."
